@startuml msb_flow
title paddock: an msb session, from boot to collected (SPEC 2.2)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor User
participant "cli.py\n`paddock launch <profile>\n~--backend msb`" as CLI
participant "sessions.py" as Sessions
participant "backends/microsandbox.py" as Backend
participant "herdr_client.py" as Client
participant "Herdr" as Herdr
participant "msb\n(one host process per VM)" as Msb
participant "guest\n(alpine microVM)" as Guest

== create the session ==

User -> CLI : paddock launch msb-live ~--backend msb
CLI -> Sessions : launch(profile, name, backend="msb")
activate Sessions
Sessions -> Sessions : create_session(profile, name, "msb")\nbackend_for("msb") -> the microsandbox module
Sessions -> Backend : prepare(profile)
activate Backend
Backend -> Backend : profile.agent must be `shell`\n(any other agent is refused here, before a VM exists:\nprovisioning an agent in the guest is the next feature)
Backend -> Backend : new_run_dir() -> <state>/runs/<timestamp>-<rand>/\nvm_handle -> paddock-<that directory's name>\nworkdir_for(profile) -> shared_dir, else run_dir/work,\nresolved, because msb mounts the source as written
Backend -> Msb : msb create ~--name paddock-<run>\n~--mount-dir <resolved workdir>:/work ~--workdir /work\n~--net-default deny [~--net-rule allow@dns\n~--net-rule allow@<domain>:tcp:443 per allowed domain]\n<image from the agent entry, else alpine>
activate Msb
Msb -> Guest : boot (175ms to usable, measured in the spike)
activate Guest
Msb --> Backend : created
Backend -> Backend : write run_dir/launch.sh:\n`msb exec ~--tty paddock-<run>`\nwrite run_dir/launch.json: vm_handle, workdir, command
Backend --> Sessions : Run(run_dir, workdir, vm_handle, command)
deactivate Backend
Sessions -> Sessions : register in <state>/sessions.json\nwith backend="msb" and vm_handle

== attach a tab (once now, again for every later tab) ==

Sessions -> Backend : load_run(run_dir) then open_pane(run, label="sbx:<session>")
activate Backend
Backend -> Client : create_tab(workdir, label)
note right
  The tab's own cwd is the HOST side of the mount,
  so the pane and the guest shell see the same files.
  No env is passed: guest variables are set on
  `msb create` with -e, not by the host tab.
end note
Client -> Herdr : herdr tab create ~--cwd <workdir> ~--label sbx:<session> ~--focus
Herdr --> Client : {"result":{"root_pane":{"pane_id":"wA:pA"}}}
Backend -> Client : run_in_pane("wA:pA", launch_line(run_dir))
Client -> Herdr : herdr pane run wA:pA\n`exec /bin/sh <run_dir>/launch.sh`
deactivate Backend
Herdr -> Msb : the pane's shell runs `msb exec ~--tty paddock-<run>`
Msb -> Guest : exec a PTY shell (20ms), in the same process namespace\nas every other tab on this session
Guest --> User : a shell in the guest, at /work
Sessions --> CLI : (session, "wA:pA")
deactivate Sessions

== collect the session ==

User -> Herdr : closes the last tab on the session
Herdr -> Sessions : remove_pane("wA:pA")
note right
  The hook that calls this on a pane closing
  is not wired up yet. Everything below it is.
end note
activate Sessions
Sessions -> Sessions : last pane, and keep_alive is not set,\nso drop the session from the registry
Sessions -> Backend : collect(run_dir)
activate Backend
Backend -> Backend : load_run(run_dir).vm_handle
Backend -> Msb : msb rm -f paddock-<run>
Msb -> Guest : destroy
deactivate Guest
deactivate Msb
note right
  Always -f: `msb rm` on its own is a silent
  no-op on a running sandbox. A VM that is
  already gone is reported on stderr, not raised:
  the session is over either way.
end note
deactivate Backend
deactivate Sessions

note over Sessions, Guest
  What the run dir keeps: launch.json and launch.sh, and work/
  when the profile shares no host directory. Collecting a session
  leaves them, because deleting a workdir would lose work.

  What the guest never had: the host filesystem. An unmounted path
  is absent, not denied, so there is no PATH shim dir and no
  deny list to get right (SPEC 4.1).
end note

@enduml
